    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need some help troubleshooting a sublimation issue. we've been running heat transfers for polyester blends but the color vibrancy is way lower than it should be and the edges look blurry. we are currently at 200c for 40 seconds with 4 bar of pressure. any idea what might be causing the poor transfer or the bleeding around the edges?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Blurry edges and dull colors in sublimation, especially on polyester blends, can be a tricky issue. It's often related to the heat application or the material itself, like a slightly less-than-perfectly-prepared substrate or a transfer paper that's starting to wear out. You might need to adjust your temperature or time, or perhaps experiment with a different type of sublimation ink or transfer paper. Sometimes, the heat needs to be a little more aggressive, like a slightly higher temperature or a longer press, to properly fuse the dye into the fibers.",
      "source": "target",
